'''assay''' (a̤-sā′), ''v.'' [< ME. ''assayen'', ''asayen'', ''asaien'' (later also by apheresis ''saye'', ''say''), < OF. ''assayer'', ''asaier'' = Pr. ''assaiar'', ''assatjar'' = Sp. ''asayar'' = It. ''assaggiare''; also, with variation of the same prefix, OF. ''essayer'' (> E. ''essay'', q. v.) = Pr. ''essaiar'', ''ensaiar'' = Cat. ''ensajar'' = Sp. ''ensayar'' = Pg. ''ensaiar''; from the noun.] '''I.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To examine by trial; put to test or trial; try the effect or merit of: as, to ''assay'' armor. [Obsolete or poetical.]
{{smaller block|Soft words to his fierce passion she ''assay’d.''
{{right|''Milton'', P. L., x. 865.}}
Here, too, our shepherd-pipes we first ''assay’d.''
{{right|''M. Arnold'', Thyrsis.}}}}
